  "output": "# Test Coverage Analysis — canon/web\n\n**Current state: zero test infrastructure.** No test framework in `package.json`, no `*.test.ts` files, no CI test step. Every function below is currently untested. I'd recommend **Vitest** (fast, native ESM/TS, works well with Next.js Server Components/route handlers) over Jest — add `vitest` + `@vitejs/plugin-react` as dev deps and a `test` script.\n\nCoverage falls into four risk tiers. I've prioritized accordingly: pure functions (trivial to test, currently 0% covered) → server business logic (needs DB mocking, highest business risk) → schema-derived logic → route handlers (integration).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pure utility functions — `lib/*.ts` (highest ROI, zero excuse not to test)\n\n### `lib/diff-chars.ts` — `diffSegments`\nUntested edge cases: equal strings, one empty string, completely disjoint strings, overlapping prefix/suffix on short strings (e.g. `\"aa\"` vs `\"a\"` — prefix/suffix math can double-count).\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"@/lib/diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns all-prefix when values are equal\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"ACME\", \"ACME\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"ACME\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a differing middle with shared head and tail\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\")).toEqual({\n      prefix: \"ACC-\", middle: \"4417\", suffix: \"\",\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles no shared prefix or suffix\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"abc\", \"xyz\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"abc\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one empty string\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"abc\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not double-count overlapping prefix/suffix on short strings\", () => {\n    // \"a\" vs \"aa\": max=1, prefix consumes the only char, suffix must not also claim it\n    expect(diffSegments(\"a\", \"aa\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"a\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles single-character differing values\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"A\", \"B\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"A\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/format.ts` — six exported functions, all untested\nEdge cases: `shortRunId` with a non-UUID-shaped string; `formatElapsed` at exact hour/minute boundaries and negative ms; `formatRelative` at the 59s/59m/23h boundaries; `formatConfidence` rounding.\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatCount, formatStat,\n  formatClockTime, formatTimestamp, formatRelative, formatConfidence,\n} from \"@/lib/format\";\n\ndescribe(\"shortRunId\", () => {\n  it(\"strips hyphens and takes 4+2 chars\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"a41f1234-c9ab-...\")).toBe(\"a41f·1c\"); // verify against real UUID\n  });\n  it(\"handles a string shorter than 6 chars without throwing\", () => {\n    expect(() => shortRunId(\"ab\")).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"formats sub-minute as mm:ss\", () => { expect(formatElapsed(5_000)).toBe(\"00:05\"); });\n  it(\"formats exactly one hour\", () => { expect(formatElapsed(3_600_000)).toBe(\"1:00:00\"); });\n  it(\"clamps negative ms to zero\", () => { expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(\"00:00\"); });\n  it(\"rolls minutes over at 59:59 → 1:00:00\", () => { expect(formatElapsed(3_599_999)).toBe(\"59:59\"); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"renders null as em dash\", () => { expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\"); });\n  it(\"renders undefined as em dash\", () => { expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\"); });\n  it(\"renders zero as '0', not em dash\", () => { expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\"); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n  it(\"says 'just now' under 60s\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:31Z\"), now)).toBe(\"just now\");\n  });\n  it(\"boundary at exactly 60s\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"1m ago\");\n  });\n  it(\"boundary at exactly 24h → days\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-07T12:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"1d ago\");\n  });\n  it(\"handles a future date without throwing (negative diff)\", () => {\n    expect(() => formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-09T12:00:00Z\"), now)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always shows two decimals\", () => { expect(formatConfidence(1)).toBe(\"1.00\"); });\n  it(\"rounds correctly\", () => { expect(formatConfidence(0.905)).toBe(\"0.91\"); }); // verify FP rounding\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/validate-value.ts` — `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`, `observedValues` (business-critical: this mirrors the engine's `validate` node — a divergence here is a correctness bug in the override guard)\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, punctuation, whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n  it(\"strips repeated legal suffixes (Pvt Ltd)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not consume 'pvt ltd' as bare 'ltd', leaving a dangling 'pvt'\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Foo Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"foo\"); // not \"foo pvt\"\n  });\n  it(\"keeps a value that IS entirely a suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n  it(\"collapses internal whitespace and NFKD-normalizes\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ac  me\")).toBe(\"ac me\");\n  });\n  it(\"folds every entry in LEGAL_SUFFIXES without throwing\", () => {\n    for (const s of LEGAL_SUFFIXES) expect(() => foldValue(`Foo ${s}`)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-4417\", [\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACME INC\", [\"Acme Inc.\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc.\" });\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an invented value\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", [\"ACC-4417\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects when neither side holds a value (orphan with no observed)\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"anything\", []).ok).toBe(false);\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"anything\", [\"\", \"  \"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"filters blank entries out of the observed list before comparing\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-4417\", [\"\", \"ACC-4417\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blanks\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"Y\"] } })).toEqual([\"X\", \"Y\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"returns empty array when both sides are empty (orphan)\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [] }, b: { values: [] } })).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/rule-trace.ts` — `deriveRuleTrace` (four distinct branches, none tested)\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"returns single not-yet-resolved step when resolution is null\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"shows apply (not propose) when a rule decided and produced a value\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"shows propose (not apply) when no rule matched but