oposed)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"falls back to bare count when action has no COUNT_NOUN entry\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"ignores non-string/non-finite values (NaN, Infinity, numeric string)\", () => {\n    // str()/num() type guards — worth asserting a numeric-string field is NOT picked up by num()\n  });\n  it(\"replaces underscore in previousStatus ('auto_applied' → 'was auto-applied')\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"appends 'note attached' without inlining the note text\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"auditDetailLine\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when parts is empty\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"joins parts with ' · '\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/api-client.ts` — `postJson`/`patchJson`/`sendJson` (network error handling, currently 0% covered — this is where \"could not reach server\" UX lives)\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { postJson, patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\nafterEach(() => vi.restoreAllMocks());\n\ndescribe(\"postJson / patchJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns ok:true with parsed data on 2xx\", async () => {\n    global.fetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(JSON.stringify({ id: 1 }), { status: 200 }));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", { a: 1 });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, data: { id: 1 } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns a friendly message when fetch throws (network down)\", async () => {\n    global.fetch = vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new TypeError(\"Failed to fetch\"));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.message).toMatch(/could not reach/i);\n  });\n\n  it(\"surfaces server error + issues on 400\", async () => {\n    global.fetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: \"Bad field\", issues: { name: \"required\" } }), { status: 400 }),\n    );\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"Bad field\", issues: { name: \"required\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to status-code message when error body has no 'error' field\", async () => {\n    global.fetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"{}\", { status: 500 }));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.message).toBe(\"Request failed (500).\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles a response body that is not valid JSON on error\", async () => {\n    global.fetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"<html>502</html>\", { status: 502 }));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false); // payload.json() rejects → caught → payload = null\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses PATCH method for patchJson\", async () => {\n    const fetchSpy = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"{}\", { status: 200 }));\n    global.fetch = fetchSpy;\n    await patchJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(fetchSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\"/api/x\", expect.objectContaining({ method: \"PATCH\" }));\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Schema-derived logic — `types/*.ts`\n\n### `types/run.ts` — `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`, `isStatKnown`, `failedStage`\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"true for complete and failed, false for every in-flight status\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n    for (const s of [\"queued\", \"extracting\", \"matching\", \"detecting\", \"resolving\"] as const) {\n      expect(isTerminalRunStatus(s)).toBe(false);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"all stats known once complete\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"all stats known once failed (partial-progress case)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"a stat is unknown before its producing stage\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"extracting\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"a stat is known once its producing stage is behind\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"entitiesA\", \"matching\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"parses stage= from the error convention\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"EngineDispatch: timeout\\nstage=dispatch\")).toBe(\"queued\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when error has no stage= marker\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"some other error\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null for a null error\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=nonsense\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"is case-insensitive on the verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=EXTRACT\")).toBe(\"extracting\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/queue.ts` — `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason`\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"conflictFieldLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 'entity absent' for orphan\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns 'N → M' for a duplicate that collapses records\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\",\n      a: { values: [\"1\",\"2\"], present: true }, b: { values: [\"1\"], present: true } })).toBe(\"2 → 1\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns 'duplicate record' when duplicate counts are equal or one side is 0\", () => {\n    // from === to, or to === 0 — both fall through to the generic label; untested branch\n  });\n  it(\"returns the raw field name for attribute/structural/cosmetic\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"severityReason\", () => {\n  it(\"orphan with children pluralizes correctly (1 child vs N children)\", () => {\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"orphan\", severity: 4, childCount: 1 })).toMatch(/1 child\\b/);\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"orphan\", severity: 4, childCount: 3 })).toMatch(/3 children/);\n  });\n  it(\"orphan with zero children\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"default branch distinguishes severity 3 vs 2 for attribute conflicts\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/rules.ts` — `orderRulesByEvaluation`, `ruleSpecificity`\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"ranks exact field + exact entityType highest (3)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"ranks wildcard/wildcard lowest (0)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"orderRulesByEvaluation\", () => {\n  it(\"sorts most specific first\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"preserves author order among equal-specificity rules (stable sort)\", () => {\n    // construct two rules with identical specificity, assert original relative order kept\n  });\n  it(\"handles an empty rule list\", () => { expect(orderRulesByEvaluation([])).toEqual([]); });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/rules.ts` — `survivorshipRuleSchema` refinement (zod `.refine`, untested)\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects strategy: prefer_source with no preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId set\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"accepts every non-prefer_source strategy without preferredSourceId\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\nAlso untested: `queueQuerySchema`'s `severities` transform (comma-split, invalid-number filtering) — e.g. `?sev=4,banana,99` should silently drop `banana` and `99` (out of 1-4 range) but keep `4`. This transform has no direct test anywhere.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"queueQuerySchema severities transform\", () => {\n  it(\"parses a valid comma list\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"4,3\" }).severities).toEqual([4, 3]);\n  });\n  it(\"drops non-numeric and out-of-range entries\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"4,banana,99\" }).severities).toEqual([4]);\n  });\n  it(\"defaults to [] when severities is absent\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({}).severities).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Server business logic — `lib/server/*.ts` (needs DB mocking — highest business risk, currently 0% covered)\n\nThese require mocking `getDb()` (drizzle) and, for auth, `@clerk/nextjs/server`. Recommend a `vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")` returning a chainable query builder stub, or run against a real test Postgres via `drizzle-orm`'s test utilities / testcontainers for true integration coverage. Skeletons below assume mocking.\n\n### `lib/server/auth.ts` — `requireReviewer`, `requireReviewerForApi`, `getReviewer` (auth boundary — a bug here is a security bug)\n\n```ts\nimport { vi, describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewerForApi\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 401 response when not authenticated\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null });\n    const gate = await requireReviewerForApi();\n    expect(gate.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!gate.ok) expect(gate.response.status).toBe(401);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns reviewer with username label when authenticated\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"falls back to email, then userId, when username/email are null\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws if auth.protect() resolves but userId is somehow null (defensive check)\", async () => {\n    // covers the explicit \"Clerk changed shape underneath us\" guard — currently unexercised\n    (authMock.protect as any).mockResolvedValue(undefined);\n    (authMock as any).mockResolvedValue({ userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/carried no userId/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when signed out, without redirecting\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when signed in\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/conflicts.ts` — `recordReview` (the most business-critical function in the codebase: every branch is an audit-trail correctness guarantee)\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 404 when the conflict does not exist\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 when no resolution exists yet (run still resolving)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"rejects approve when proposedValue is empty (escalated with no proposal)\", async () => {\n    // this is the guard: \"Approving nothing is not a decision\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects override with an invented value not in observed[]\", async () => {\n    // asserts checkObservedValue integration — 400 + reason from validate-value\n  });\n\n  it(\"stores overrideValue as the folded/matched observed value, not as typed\", async () => {\n    // e.g. reviewer types \"ACME INC\", stored value should be the observed \"Acme Inc.\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"clears overrideValue when action is approve or reject\", async () => {\n    // regression guard: \"row never shows a chosen value that no longer stands\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"writes reviewedBy from the session reviewer, ignoring any client-supplied value\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"appends an audit entry with previousStatus set to the prior resolution status\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"reject action sets chosenValue to null in the audit detail\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"approve/override sets chosenValue to the resolved value in audit detail\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"includes the note in audit detail only when non-empty\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\nAlso untested: `toQueueRow`'s orphan-presence logic (`present: !isOrphan || aValues.length > 0`), `sourceName` fallback to `\"unknown source\"` when a conflict's entity belongs to neither run source (explicitly called out in the code comment as \"an engine bug\" — worth a regression test precisely because it's a defensive branch nobody expects to hit), and `splitValues` (newline-split, blank-line filtering, all-blank input).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"splitValues\", () => {\n  it(\"splits on newlines and trims each part\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"filters out blank lines\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns [] for an empty string\", () => { expect(splitValues(\"\")).toEqual([]); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"toQueueRow orphan presence\", () => {\n  it(\"side is present:false when class is orphan and values are empty\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"side is present:true for orphan when values ARE non-empty (edge: partial data)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"non-orphan classes are always present regardless of values\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/runs.ts`, `lib/server/rulesets.ts`, `lib/server/export.ts`, `lib/server/entities.ts` — all 0% covered\n\nHighest-value gaps:\n- `getSeverityBreakdown` — drops a severity value outside 1..4 (`severitySchema.safeParse` guard) rather than throwing. **Untested defensive branch.**\n- `createRulesetVersion` — version increments correctly on first save (`highest ?? 0) + 1`), and the previous active ruleset is deactivated. Concurrency behavior (advisory lock) can't be unit tested but the version-numbering logic can be.\n- `failUndispatchedRun` — the `WHERE status = 'queued'` guard: a run already advanced past `queued` must NOT be overwritten by a late dispatch failure. **This guard is exactly the kind of thing a unit test with a mocked/fake DB should assert was included in the WHERE clause, or an integration test should assert behaviorally.**\n- `buildRunExport` — section-gating logic: `hierarchy` implicitly needs `decisions` loaded, but `decisions` section is only *attached to output* when explicitly requested. Test that requesting `hierarchy` alone does NOT include `decisions` in the response.\n- `applyDecisions` — `reparented` flag: only true when resolved parent differs from original; untested when `resolved === account.parentExternalId` (rule fired but produced the same value it started with).\n- `estimateExportBytes` — trivial but untested arithmetic; test with a subset of sections to confirm unselected sections don't contribute.\n- `decisionsToCsv` / `csvCell` — CSV-injection-adjacent escaping: values containing commas, quotes, `\\r\\n`. **Untested and security-adjacent** (a malicious `rationale` or note field containing `\",\\r\\n` must not break the CSV structure).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"buildRunExport section gating\", () => {\n  it(\"requesting only 'hierarchy' does not attach a 'decisions' key\", async () => {\n    const result = await buildRunExport(mockRun, \"reviewer\", [\"hierarchy\"]);\n    expect(result.decisions).toBeUndefined();\n    expect(result.hierarchy).toBeDefined();\n  });\n  it(\"requesting only 'orphans' does not compute hierarchy/decisions\", async () => { /* assert underlying queries not called */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv / csvCell\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes a field containing a comma\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"a,b\")).toBe('\"a,b\"'); });\n  it(\"escapes embedded double quotes by doubling them\", () => { expect(csvCell('say \"hi\"')).toBe('\"say \"\"hi\"\"\"'); });\n  it(\"quotes a field containing \\\\r\\\\n\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"line1\\r\\nline2\")).toBe('\"line1\\r\\nline2\"'); });\n  it(\"leaves a plain value unquoted\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"ACME\")).toBe(\"ACME\"); });\n  it(\"renders null as empty string\", () => { expect(csvCell(null)).toBe(\"\"); });\n  it(\"full CSV output ends with a trailing CRLF\", () => { expect(decisionsToCsv([])).toMatch(/\\r\\n$/); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failUndispatchedRun\", () => {\n  it(\"does not overwrite a run that has already left 'queued'\", async () => {\n    // seed a run with status: \"matching\", call failUndispatchedRun, assert status unchanged\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"first save for a new name gets version 1\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"subsequent save increments from the highest existing version\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"deactivates the previously active ruleset (any name)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getSeverityBreakdown\", () => {\n  it(\"drops rows whose severity is outside 1..4 rather than throwing\", async () => {\n    // mock DB row with severity: 7, assert it's excluded from the breakdown and totals stay correct\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/server/engine.ts` — `startRun`, `fetchEngineStatus` (network boundary to a separate process — timeouts and malformed responses are exactly what breaks in production)\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when ENGINE_URL is not set\", async () => {\n    delete process.env.ENGINE_URL;\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-id\")).rejects.toThrow(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n  it(\"throws with a timeout-specific message on AbortSignal timeout\", async () => {\n    // mock fetch to reject with a DOMException named \"TimeoutError\"\n  });\n  it(\"throws when the engine responds non-2xx, including response body in message\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"throws when the engine responds 200 but with a body that fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    // e.g. { accepted: false } or missing runId — engineStartRunResponseSchema mismatch\n  });\n  it(\"succeeds silently on a valid 200 response\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not throw) on network failure\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns null on non-2xx response\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns null when the response body fails schema validation\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns parsed status on success\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. API route handlers — integration tests (0% covered)\n\nThese need Next.js route-handler test harness (`Request`/`RouteContext` mocks) plus mocked auth + server functions. Highest-value scenarios per route:\n\n### `PATCH /api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution`\n```ts\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:id/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s on a non-UUID conflictId path param ('banana')\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s on an invalid body (missing action)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s on override action with empty overrideValue\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated, BEFORE reading the body's business meaning\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"passes through recordReview's 404/409/400 as the corresponding HTTP status\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"200s with { conflictId, status, reviewedBy } on success\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\nNote the auth-vs-body-parse ordering: currently `parseJson` runs **before** `requireReviewerForApi`. Worth a test asserting that an unauthenticated request with a malformed body still returns a definitive status (400 vs 401 — whichever the code path actually returns first) — this is exactly the kind of ordering that regresses silently during refactors.\n\n### `POST /api/runs`\n```ts\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId === sourceBId\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId does not exist\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s when rulesetId does not exist\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"201s and returns runId on success, with an engine dispatch\", async () => { /* mock startRun to resolve */ });\n  it(\"still 201s when engine dispatch fails, but marks the run failed + appends run_failed audit\", async () => {\n    // mock startRun to throw EngineUnreachableError — this is the most important untested branch:\n    // response is 201 even though the run silently failed. Assert failUndispatchedRun + appendAudit both called.\n  });\n  it(\"rethrows a non-EngineUnreachableError from startRun rather than swallowing it\", async () => {\n    // the `if (!(cause instanceof EngineUnreachableError)) throw cause;` branch — currently unexercised\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `GET /api/runs/[runId]/export`\n```ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/runs/:id/export\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on invalid format (not json/csv)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s on unknown section name in ?sections=\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"de-duplicates and canonically orders sections regardless of query order\", async () => {\n    // ?sections=decisions,hierarchy,decisions should produce [hierarchy, decisions] once each\n  });\n  it(\"400s on an empty sections list (?sections=)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"404s when runId is a well-formed UUID but no run exists\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"csv format returns only the decisions section regardless of ?sections=\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"sets content-disposition filename derived from shortRunId with the interpunct stripped\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `GET /api/audit/export`\n```ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/audit/export\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on an invalid action enum value\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"404s when runId is well-formed but not found\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"omits the run scope from filename when no runId given\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"CSV includes both flattened detail and raw detailJson columns\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `GET /api/conflicts`\n```ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/conflicts\", () => {\n  it(\"400s with the first Zod issue message on an invalid query\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns run:null, conflicts:[] when no runs exist yet (no-runs state)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integration test gaps (cross-module flows, none exist today)\n\n1. **End-to-end review flow**: create run → seed conflict+resolution → PATCH override with an invalid value → 400 → PATCH override with a valid value → 200 → GET audit export → assert the audit CSV contains the override with correct `previousStatus`.\n2. **Ruleset versioning immutability**: create run under ruleset v1 → save ruleset as v2 → assert `getRunDetail` for the old run still reports `rulesetVersion: 1` and the queue's `appliedRuleStrategy` resolves from the run's own ruleset, not the currently-active one. This is a specifically-called-out design invariant (`lib/server/conflicts.ts` comment) with no test guarding it.\n3. **Auth boundary end-to-end**: hit every route handler unauthenticated and assert 401 (not 500, not a redirect leaking HTML into a JSON client) — a single parametrized test over all routes would catch a handler that forgets the gate.\n4. **`validate-value.ts` ↔ engine parity**: the code comments explicitly warn `engine/pipeline/normalize.py`'s `LEGAL_SUFFIXES` must match `lib/validate-value.ts`'s list exactly, \"or these two must stay in lockstep.\" There's no test (even a manual doc pointer) verifying this cross-repo. Worth either a shared fixture or, at minimum, a test that snapshots the suffix list so a change is caught in review.\n5. **Export sizing vs. actual export**: `getExportSizing` counts should match the actual row counts `buildRunExport` produces for the same run — currently two independent code paths with no test tying them together (a drift here shows a reviewer the wrong pre-download estimate).\n\n---\n\n## Priority order if coverage work is scoped incrementally\n\n1. `lib/validate-value.ts`, `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` — business-critical, override-value-injection guard\n2. `lib/server/auth.ts` — security boundary\n3. `lib/api-client.ts`, `lib/server/engine.ts` — network failure handling, currently the most likely source of unhandled production errors\n4. `lib/format.ts`, `lib/audit-detail.ts`, `types/run.ts` derived functions — cheap, pure, high branch count\n5. Route handler integration tests — catches auth/validation ordering regressions\n6. `lib/server/export.ts` CSV escaping — security-adjacent, currently untested\n",
