        "title": "`lib/server/runs.ts`, `lib/server/rulesets.ts`, `lib/server/export.ts`, `lib/server/entities.ts` — all 0% covered",
        "content": "\nHighest-value gaps:\n- `getSeverityBreakdown` — drops a severity value outside 1..4 (`severitySchema.safeParse` guard) rather than throwing. **Untested defensive branch.**\n- `createRulesetVersion` — version increments correctly on first save (`highest ?? 0) + 1`), and the previous active ruleset is deactivated. Concurrency behavior (advisory lock) can't be unit tested but the version-numbering logic can be.\n- `failUndispatchedRun` — the `WHERE status = 'queued'` guard: a run already advanced past `queued` must NOT be overwritten by a late dispatch failure. **This guard is exactly the kind of thing a unit test with a mocked/fake DB should assert was included in the WHERE clause, or an integration test should assert behaviorally.**\n- `buildRunExport` — section-gating logic: `hierarchy` implicitly needs `decisions` loaded, but `decisions` section is only *attached to output* when explicitly requested. Test that requesting `hierarchy` alone does NOT include `decisions` in the response.\n- `applyDecisions` — `reparented` flag: only true when resolved parent differs from original; untested when `resolved === account.parentExternalId` (rule fired but produced the same value it started with).\n- `estimateExportBytes` — trivial but untested arithmetic; test with a subset of sections to confirm unselected sections don't contribute.\n- `decisionsToCsv` / `csvCell` — CSV-injection-adjacent escaping: values containing commas, quotes, `\\r\\n`. **Untested and security-adjacent** (a malicious `rationale` or note field containing `\",\\r\\n` must not break the CSV structure).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"buildRunExport section gating\", () => {\n  it(\"requesting only 'hierarchy' does not attach a 'decisions' key\", async () => {\n    const result = await buildRunExport(mockRun, \"reviewer\", [\"hierarchy\"]);\n    expect(result.decisions).toBeUndefined();\n    expect(result.hierarchy).toBeDefined();\n  });\n  it(\"requesting only 'orphans' does not compute hierarchy/decisions\", async () => { /* assert underlying queries not called */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv / csvCell\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes a field containing a comma\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"a,b\")).toBe('\"a,b\"'); });\n  it(\"escapes embedded double quotes by doubling them\", () => { expect(csvCell('say \"hi\"')).toBe('\"say \"\"hi\"\"\"'); });\n  it(\"quotes a field containing \\\\r\\\\n\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"line1\\r\\nline2\")).toBe('\"line1\\r\\nline2\"'); });\n  it(\"leaves a plain value unquoted\", () => { expect(csvCell(\"ACME\")).toBe(\"ACME\"); });\n  it(\"renders null as empty string\", () => { expect(csvCell(null)).toBe(\"\"); });\n  it(\"full CSV output ends with a trailing CRLF\", () => { expect(decisionsToCsv([])).toMatch(/\\r\\n$/); });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failUndispatchedRun\", () => {\n  it(\"does not overwrite a run that has already left 'queued'\", async () => {\n    // seed a run with status: \"matching\", call failUndispatchedRun, assert status unchanged\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"first save for a new name gets version 1\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"subsequent save increments from the highest existing version\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"deactivates the previously active ruleset (any name)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getSeverityBreakdown\", () => {\n  it(\"drops rows whose severity is outside 1..4 rather than throwing\", async () => {\n    // mock DB row with severity: 7, assert it's excluded from the breakdown and totals stay correct\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
